description:
Objective: the pure, network-free admission half of CQ-R11e3's offline npm dependency cache. It turns a candidate's untrusted package-lock.json files into the exact, deduplicated list of registry tarballs the host may fetch. Every other entry kind is refused with a fixed code BEFORE anything is downloaded. Split from CQ-R11e3 (task-ab029075) by architect-4ae016fb on 2026-10-30 to keep both slices under the 400-line review cap. CQ-R11e3's buildDependencyCache calls this export first, before any filesystem or fetch call.

Deliverable: a new scripts/local-runner/dependency-cache.mjs exporting:
- admitLockfiles({ lockfiles, cpu }). It returns, synchronously, a deeply frozen { dirs, packages }:
  - dirs: the lockfile dirs, sorted by UTF-8 bytes, '.' for the root;
  - packages: [{ integrity, sha512, url }], one per distinct integrity, sorted by sha512. sha512 is the digest as 128 lowercase hex. url is the smallest canonical URL among the entries sharing that integrity.
- dependencyError(code), with a fixed message per code (as snapshotError in source-snapshot.mjs).
- The constants MAX_LOCKFILES = 16, MAX_LOCKFILE_BYTES = 16_777_216 and MAX_DEPENDENCY_PACKAGES = MAX_IMPORT_ENTRIES - 1. The one spare entry is the tree's moe-dependencies.json in CQ-R11e3.

Rules:
- Input: exact keys {lockfiles, cpu}. cpu is 'x64' or 'arm64'. lockfiles is a real Array of 1-16 exact-key {dir, bytes} records. dir is '.' or a path that source-snapshot.mjs validateImportPath returns unchanged, and dirs are unique. bytes is a Uint8Array or Buffer of at most MAX_LOCKFILE_BYTES. Read each property once.
- Each lockfile is fatal-UTF-8 JSON of a plain object, with lockfileVersion exactly 2 or 3 and packages a plain object.
- Every packages key except '' (the root project) must be a node_modules location: one or more `node_modules/<name>` segments, where a name is a scoped or unscoped npm name of [A-Za-z0-9._~-] that does not start with '.' or '_'. Use a linear-time regex. Workspace folder keys and anything else are refused.
- Skipped, never checked further and never fetched:
  - inBundle:true entries, which ship inside their parent's verified tarball;
  - optional:true entries whose os excludes 'linux' or whose cpu excludes the given cpu. Use npm-install-checks checkList semantics: a string or an array, 'any', and '!x' negation. libc is never filtered: an extra package is harmless, a missing one fails the offline install.
- Every other entry must have:
  - link not true;
  - a semver version;
  - resolved EXACTLY equal to `https://registry.npmjs.org/<name>/-/<unscoped name>-<version>.tgz`. name is entry.name for an npm alias, else the location's last name. Plain string equality: no URL normalization.
  - integrity that is exactly one canonical `sha512-<86 base64 chars>==` token, decoding to 64 bytes whose re-encoding is the same text.
- Refusals use fixed text that never carries a URL, path or body:
  - DEPENDENCY_INPUT_INVALID;
  - DEPENDENCY_LOCKFILE_INVALID;
  - DEPENDENCY_LOCATION_INVALID;
  - DEPENDENCY_SOURCE_UNSUPPORTED: link, git, file, http, another host, userinfo, a port, a query or fragment, an alias-to-tarball or other non-canonical resolved, a missing resolved or version;
  - DEPENDENCY_INTEGRITY_INVALID: missing, sha1, multi-hash, the wrong length, or non-canonical base64;
  - DEPENDENCY_LIMIT_EXCEEDED: a lockfile over MAX_LOCKFILE_BYTES, or more distinct packages than MAX_DEPENDENCY_PACKAGES.
  An unexpected throw (a getter or a Proxy) becomes DEPENDENCY_INPUT_INVALID. There is never a partial result.
- Pure: no filesystem, network, process, npm or candidate code.

Measured on 2026-10-30, these rules admit every entry of packages/moe-daemon, moe-proxy and moe-vscode's lockfiles. They refuse packages/moe-claude-plugin's 49 entries that have no resolved, which is known and out of scope.

Tests: rows DA1-DA5 in scripts/tests/local-runner-check.test.mjs, which is already in CI's local-runner list.

NOT in scope:
- downloading, the cacache tree, OFFLINE_INSTALL_ARGS and the npm end-to-end row (CQ-R11e3);
- guest streaming and install (CQ-R11e4/e5);
- workspaces support;
- .moe edits, or any verified-local or isolation claim.

Verification command (fresh, exit 0 required): node --test scripts/tests/local-runner-check.test.mjs (on WSL: env -i HOME="$HOME" PATH=/home/sysadmin/.nvm/versions/node/v24.21.0/bin:/usr/bin:/bin)

planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
Patterns to mirror from source-snapshot.mjs: isRecord, the VIEW_PROTOTYPES and viewLength intrinsic getter, snapshotError plus the OWN_ERRORS WeakSet, a length read once below a bound, and index reads (no slice).

local-runner-check.test.mjs uses static top-level imports, so a missing module fails the WHOLE file; that is the red signal. Its rows: E1-E8, K1-K9, C1-C7. CQ-R11e1 (task-b799056d, which now dependsOn this task) and R11e3 edit the file after this task lands.

The architect measured these rules on 2026-10-30 against the repo lockfiles:
- daemon: 157 entries ok, 155 unique, 73 optional-platform;
- proxy: 113 ok;
- vscode: 339 ok;
- claude-plugin: 49 entries without resolved, which are refused.
npm checkList semantics are copied from npm-install-checks.
